{"explanation":"Strengthen the existing MasterKey lifecycle regression test without changing its entry point or retained encryption/decryption expectations: the wrong-password path must fail with the existing concrete AES/GCM authentication exception rather than silently passing if decryption unexpectedly succeeds.","review_assumptions":["On supported Android providers, decrypting this MasterKey record with an incorrect password continues to surface javax.crypto.AEADBadTagException for AES/GCM authentication failure.","Persisted file-format compatibility is preserved by the coordinated production changes and is outside the scope of this test-only edit."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"high","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/MasterKeyTest.java","original_code":"    @Test
    public void test() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        String pwd = "MyM4sterPassw0rd";
        String wrongpwd = "Incorrectpwd";

        MasterKey orig = MasterKey.generate(pwd);
        MasterKey read = new Gson().fromJson(new Gson().toJson(orig), MasterKey.class);

        Assert.assertArrayEquals(orig.decrypt(pwd).getEncoded(), read.decrypt(pwd).getEncoded());
        assertEquals(orig.decrypt(pwd).getAlgorithm(), "AES");
        assertEquals(read.decrypt(pwd).getAlgorithm(), "AES");

        try {
            orig.decrypt(wrongpwd);
        } catch (AEADBadTagException e) {
            // Expected
            // javax.crypto.AEADBadTagException:
            // error:1e000065:Cipher functions:OPENSSL_internal:BAD_DECRYPT
        }
    }","edit_kind":"test","corrected_code":"    @Test
    public void test() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        String pwd = "MyM4sterPassw0rd";
        String wrongpwd = "Incorrectpwd";

        MasterKey orig = MasterKey.generate(pwd);
        MasterKey read = new Gson().fromJson(new Gson().toJson(orig), MasterKey.class);

        Assert.assertArrayEquals(orig.decrypt(pwd).getEncoded(), read.decrypt(pwd).getEncoded());
        assertEquals(orig.decrypt(pwd).getAlgorithm(), "AES");
        assertEquals(read.decrypt(pwd).getAlgorithm(), "AES");

        try {
            orig.decrypt(wrongpwd);
            Assert.fail("Decrypting a MasterKey with an incorrect password must fail authentication");
        } catch (AEADBadTagException e) {
            // Expected
            // javax.crypto.AEADBadTagException:
            // error:1e000065:Cipher functions:OPENSSL_internal:BAD_DECRYPT
        }
    }","reason":"Retains the existing MasterKey.generate/decrypt round-trip, encoding, and AES-algorithm assertions while making the existing wrong-password AES/GCM authentication expectation enforceable. This exercises the unchanged MasterKey entry point after the coordinated AES KeyGenerator lifecycle change without asserting ciphertext, nonce, PBKDF2 output, or persisted representation.","symbol":"MasterKeyTest.test"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["MasterKeyTest preserves its existing MasterKey.generate(String) and decrypt(String) round-trip assertions for key encoding and AES algorithm.","MasterKeyTest now verifies that the existing wrong-password path concretely fails with AEADBadTagException rather than allowing successful decryption."],"required_contracts":["MasterKey retains its existing generate(String) and decrypt(String) entry points and checked-exception behavior.","MasterKey.generate(String) supplies an AES KeyGenerator-origin protected key to the unchanged EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) API.","The coordinated production changes preserve the existing serialized MasterKey representation and decryptability expectations."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/MasterKeyTest.java","required_tests":["Run MasterKeyTest on supported Android providers to verify generated MasterKey serialization/deserialization decrypts to matching AES key material and an incorrect password throws AEADBadTagException.","Run the coordinated EncryptedKeyTest and KeyStoreAccessTest instrumentation coverage after compiling all androidTest sources."]}
